# Vite loads .env.local for EVERY mode, including production builds, and it
# overrides plain .env. .env.local (gitignored, developer-machine-only) has
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000 for local dev work against a local
# backend — but that meant every `npm run build` run on this machine (used
# to produce the Android APK) baked http://localhost:5000 into the app
# instead of the real Railway backend. The APK doesn't fail with a CORS
# error in that case — it fails with a flat "failed to fetch", because it's
# trying to reach a server on the phone itself that doesn't exist.
#
# .env.production is loaded AFTER .env.local for production builds (mode
# defaults to "production" for `vite build`), so it wins and pins this
# permanently regardless of whatever is in .env.local. This file is safe to
# commit — it contains no secrets, only the public production API endpoint.
VITE_API_URL=https://graceful-vitality-production-e097.up.railway.app
